```js
const PURGE_AFTER_DAYS = 45;
const DAY_MS = 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000;
const NEVER_PURGE_STATUSES = new Set(["legal_hold", "dispute"]);

export function shouldPurge(account, now) {
  if (NEVER_PURGE_STATUSES.has(account.status)) {
    return false;
  }
  if (account.deletedAt === null || account.deletedAt === undefined) {
    return false;
  }
  const elapsedMs = now.getTime() - account.deletedAt.getTime();
  return elapsedMs >= PURGE_AFTER_DAYS * DAY_MS;
}
```

The rules come from the earlier sessions:
- **Never purged:** status `legal_hold` or `dispute`, regardless of deletion date.
- **Purged:** soft-deleted accounts (`deletedAt` set) once 45 days have passed since deletion. Exactly 45 days counts as purgeable.
- **Kept:** accounts that were never deleted.

I picked the 45-day cutoff as an elapsed-milliseconds comparison, so the result doesn't depend on calendar months or time zones. The module follows the existing `export const` style in `src/index.mjs`.

